    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n567" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγκοινα</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγκον-ψᾰ,</span> cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγκών</span>) poet. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγκάλη,</span>
		only in pl., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ζηνὸς . . ἐν ἀγκοίνησιν ἰαν́εις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					14.213
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				11.261
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				245
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.954.2
			</span></i>. metaph., <i>anything enfolding,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν χθονὸς ἀγκοίναις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.398
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Jul.
			</span></i> Aegypt.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				3.34
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>halyard,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				2.794b20
			</span></i>, al., prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Alc.
				18.9
			</span></i>.</div>
